<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">XGL Services · The Lab</div><h1 class="display">Practical help<br>for the whole<br>business.</h1><p class="hero-copy">XGL helps independent builders improve how they attract opportunities, manage relationships, follow up, serve customers, operate internally, and grow without surrendering their identity.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/assessment">Start the Assessment</a><a class="button button-outline" href="#builds">See Builds &amp; Pricing</a></div></div></section>

<section class="section cream"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow orange">Core Capabilities</div><h2 class="section-title">What we actually do.</h2></div><div class="copy">XGL is intentionally broader than a conventional marketing agency. We connect the commercial and operating work that customers experience as one company—even when it spans several departments.</div></div><div class="cap-grid expanded-caps"><article class="cap-card"><h3>Strategy &amp; Growth Consulting</h3><p>Clarify positioning, constraints, priorities, opportunities, and the practical route forward.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Customer Acquisition</h3><p>Improve field marketing, lead intake, campaign structure, relationship development, and the path from attention to conversation.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>CRM &amp; Automation</h3><p>Implement and manage GoHighLevel-based CRM, pipelines, follow-up, communications, ownership, and useful automation.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Sales Process &amp; Follow-Up</h3><p>Give opportunities a visible path, clear responsibility, timely follow-up, and a better chance of becoming durable customer relationships.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Customer Experience</h3><p>Strengthen the journey from first signal through quoting, delivery, support, retention, and referral.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Operations &amp; Process</h3><p>Reduce avoidable friction, document critical work, improve handoffs, and build systems that do not depend on heroic memory.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Events &amp; Physical Conversion</h3><p>Connect Expo strategy, QR assets, signage, intake paths, field conversations, and post-event follow-up.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Research &amp; Intelligence</h3><p>Translate industry, market, regulatory, event, technology, and operating terrain into decisions builders can use.</p></article><article class="cap-card"><h3>Long-Term Stewardship</h3><p>Provide ongoing practical support where strategy, systems, relationships, and operating resilience need continued attention.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="section teal"><div class="wrap intensive"><div><div class="eyebrow">First Engagement</div><h2 class="section-title">Start with<br>the terrain.</h2><p class="copy">The Growth Terrain Assessment gives XGL enough signal to understand the business problem before recommending a package, project, or platform.</p></div><div class="copy"><p>Where deeper diagnosis is useful, a separately scoped Growth Terrain Intensive may examine the revenue system, customer journey, lead handling, CRM and follow-up, operating friction, digital presence, Expo conversion, and immediate priorities.</p><ul><li>Human review of the current situation</li><li>Constraints and opportunities identified</li><li>Practical priorities before machinery</li><li>A recommendation matched to the actual terrain</li><li>No automatic assumption that a large build is required</li></ul><a class="button" href="/assessment">Begin the Assessment</a></div></div></section>

<section id="builds" class="section cream"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow orange">Project-Based Implementation</div><h2 class="section-title">Basic &amp;<br>Full Stack Builds</h2></div><div class="copy" style="align-self:end">These are tailored implementation engagements, not one-size-fits-all boxes. The assessment determines fit; the written proposal establishes the actual scope.</div></div><div class="build-grid"><article class="build-card"><small>Basic Build · Standard Retail</small><div class="price">$5,495</div><p>Focused implementation around the highest-priority customer-acquisition, revenue-flow, CRM, follow-up, or operating-system needs identified during recon.</p></article><article class="build-card dark-card"><small>Full Stack Build · Standard Retail</small><div class="price">$10,495</div><p>A broader connected build spanning the agreed combination of strategy, intake, CRM, pipeline, follow-up, communications, reporting, customer experience, and team ownership.</p></article></div><div class="promo-note"><strong>Verified Expo promotional pricing:</strong> Basic Build $3,995 · Full Stack Build $8,495. Promotional pricing is limited to qualifying Expo opportunities and is not universally available. Eligibility and scope must be confirmed by XGL in writing.</div><p class="fineprint">Published prices are reference investments for the named builds, not universal quotations or guaranteed inclusions. Final deliverables, schedule, third-party costs, ongoing services, and investment are established after assessment and confirmed in a written proposal. Physical products, custom operating systems or applications, lead-generation packages, paid media, and other add-ons are separate unless explicitly bundled in writing.</p><a class="button" href="/assessment">Map Your Growth Terrain</a></div></section>

<section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-grid compact-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">How Engagements Work</div><h2 class="section-title">Project when needed.<br>Support when useful.</h2></div><div class="copy" style="align-self:end">A client should always be able to tell what kind of relationship is being proposed and what stage a capability has reached.</div></div><div class="status-grid"><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label live">Available now</span><h3>Project Engagements</h3><p>Assessments, consulting, CRM and revenue-system builds, customer-experience work, process improvement, event systems, and other agreed implementation.</p></article><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label live">Available by agreement</span><h3>Ongoing Stewardship</h3><p>Continued management, advisory support, system refinement, research, relationship development, and operational help where recurring work is justified.</p></article><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label developing">Separately scoped</span><h3>Specialized Builds</h3><p>Custom applications or operating systems, physical assets, lead-generation programs, integrations, and engineering-heavy work require their own scope and pricing.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="section cream"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow orange">The Wider XGL Ecosystem</div><h2 class="section-title">Real foundations.<br>Honest status.</h2></div><div class="copy">Some XGL capabilities are operating today. Others are expanding or being developed deliberately. We will not market a roadmap as a finished product.</div></div><div class="status-grid light-status"><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label live">Live &amp; expanding</span><h3>Command Central</h3><p>Public Field Signals, event intelligence, and Watchtower-based industry intelligence are online and growing.</p><a class="text-link dark-link" href="/command-central">Enter Command Central →</a></article><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label active">Active foundation</span><h3>One Rising Sun</h3><p>A selective, values-aligned partnership and membership network with its founding framework and first member relationships in place.</p><a class="text-link dark-link" href="/one-rising-sun">Explore the network →</a></article><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label developing">In development</span><h3>Builder Catalog &amp; Parts Intelligence</h3><p>Portable digital vendor catalogs, product data, fitment intelligence, controlled pricing, and supported distribution for independent builders and manufacturers.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="center-statement teal"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">The Working Rule</div><h2 class="section-title">Use the right tool.<br>Solve the real problem.</h2><p class="copy">XGL uses technology—including AI—where it creates genuine leverage. We do not install machinery because it is fashionable, and we do not create complexity merely to justify a recurring bill.</p><div class="hero-actions centered-actions"><a class="button" href="/assessment">Start with the Terrain</a><a class="button button-outline" href="/faq">Read the Straight Answers</a></div></div></section>
